# `public/data/catalog.bin.gz` is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the whole catalog —
# ~7 MB of typed arrays and two dates, no absolute paths and no local state. The app
# runs on it here, GitHub Pages serves it from there, and `npm run update-snapshot`
# rewrites it in place. The only copy made of it is the one `update-snapshot.js` keeps
# before replacing the file, so a refresh can be undone. Those live here.
backups/

# Local scratch a working session leaves behind: probe scripts, throwaway browser
# profiles, logs. Keep it under .probe/ — a browser profile holds real logins, and
# none of this belongs in a release.
.probe/

node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
